WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.887
Lab 2 is the runbook itself,
and nobody has run it yet.

2
00:00:03.887 --> 00:00:08.932
You need a test environment for each provider
the agency enables, never production,

3
00:00:08.932 --> 00:00:12.148
with each reader already
granted in its module's Lab 2,

4
00:00:12.148 --> 00:00:13.976
and an approved change record.

5
00:00:13.976 --> 00:00:18.640
You also need people: someone who can
create policy and role assignments for the

6
00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:22.881
alert policy, a reviewer who isn't the
operator to approve each plan's hash,

7
00:00:22.881 --> 00:00:25.425
and a Windows account
for the scheduled run.

8
00:00:25.425 --> 00:00:30.131
Then follow Stage 1: fill and check
the settings file, sign in each reader,

9
00:00:30.131 --> 00:00:35.076
run the pre-flight, enable the providers
one at a time with a cross-check each,

10
00:00:35.076 --> 00:00:40.101
route as a dry run, run the smoke test,
apply the alert policy with its approved

11
00:00:40.101 --> 00:00:45.525
hash, schedule the weekly run, check the
stage's evidence and rehearse the rollback.

12
00:00:45.525 --> 00:00:51.363
Stage 2, production, comes only when
every go/no-go criterion passes.

13
00:00:51.363 --> 00:00:55.550
To back it out, Step 1.9
applies the approved rollback.

14
00:00:55.550 --> 00:00:58.250
The state, runs and evidence are kept.
